; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; web_check — the REAL browser seam (full rocq-runtime kernel).
;
;   dune build web/web_check.bc   links the whole pipeline to bytecode.
;
; web/build-real.sh then runs wasm_of_ocaml over web_check.bc TWICE — the
; universal --effects=cps engine and the --effects=jspi upgrade engine — to
; produce the shipped WebAssembly engines. There is no js_of_ocaml backend.
;
; To produce a build that actually RUNS, the .bc is compiled against the
; coerce-32bit OCAMLPATH overlay built by web/build-real.sh (a patched,
; Int64-backed rocq-runtime kernel.cma). Built against the stock native
; rocq-runtime it instead TRAPS at startup on the kernel's `Sys.word_size = 64`
; assertion (kernel/uint63_63.ml) — see BACKEND.md sections 1c-2. Always use
; web/build-real.sh.
;
; The wasm engine's custom C primitives (float64, threads, VM init, getpid, and
; the ~30 zarith ml_z_*) come from web/rocq_shims.wat (WebAssembly), which
; delegates arbitrary-precision arithmetic to the JS BigInt helpers in
; web/rocq_zarith.js. wasm_of_ocaml resolves OCaml `external` C primitives from
; the wasm runtime ONLY (a JS //Provides fragment becomes a throwing dummy), so
; there are no js_of_ocaml-style javascript_files.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The Corelib prelude declares ML modules (cc, firstorder, number_string_notation,
; ltac, tauto) and stdlib/mathcomp need more. The wasm build has no Dynlink, so
; every plugin the mounted .vo can [Declare ML Module] must be STATICALLY linked
; here (its tactic/notation/grammar extensions register at module init) and its
; findlib package resolved from a stripped META in the VFS (web_check.ml mounts
; one with archive/plugin removed, so Rocq's findlib lookup succeeds but loads
; nothing — the code is already linked). Adding a plugin here is what makes the
; corresponding [Declare ML Module] a no-op instead of a Dynlink failure.
;
; `js_of_ocaml` stays in (libraries): web_check.ml uses the Js_of_ocaml module
; (Js.Unsafe / Sys_js), whose API wasm_of_ocaml also provides. Only the js_of_ocaml
; *backend* (the `js` mode + javascript_files) is gone.
(executable
 (name web_check)
 (modules web_check)
 (modes byte)
 (link_flags (-linkall))
 (libraries
  rocq_comparator js_of_ocaml yojson findlib
  rocq-runtime.plugins.ltac
  rocq-runtime.plugins.cc_core
  rocq-runtime.plugins.cc
  rocq-runtime.plugins.firstorder_core
  rocq-runtime.plugins.firstorder
  rocq-runtime.plugins.number_string_notation
  rocq-runtime.plugins.tauto
  ; Stdlib (Milestone 2): Arith/ZArith/Reals/Lia/ring/field/nsatz.
  rocq-runtime.plugins.ring
  rocq-runtime.plugins.micromega_core
  rocq-runtime.plugins.micromega
  rocq-runtime.plugins.zify
  rocq-runtime.plugins.btauto
  rocq-runtime.plugins.rtauto
  rocq-runtime.plugins.nsatz_core
  rocq-runtime.plugins.nsatz
  ; Phase 2: HB/mathcomp .vos load elpi objects — static-link the elpi plugin
  ; (its Libobject loaders register at engine init; stripped META makes the
  ; mathcomp Declare ML Module a no-op over this already-linked code). On wasm
  ; Sys.int_size=31 => elpi hash_bits=30, matching the patched-native .vos.
  rocq-elpi.elpi
  ; The mathcomp .vos carry ssreflect generic arguments (e.g. the "ssrhintarg"
  ; Dyn tag of Ltac `done`) and rocq-elpi app objects; every plugin whose
  ; objects appear in a shipped .vo/.vos must be linked here, or loading fails
  ; with "Unknown dynamic tag" (Declare ML Module is a no-op over the stripped META).
  rocq-runtime.plugins.ssreflect
  rocq-runtime.plugins.ssrmatching
  rocq-elpi.coercion
  rocq-elpi.cs
  rocq-elpi.tc
  rocq-runtime.plugins.funind
  ; mathcomp algebra's ring/field/lia tactics declare the standalone micromega
  ; plugin (opam rocq-micromega-plugin, user-contrib/micromega_plugin), distinct
  ; from rocq-runtime's; stage-packs.sh ships its stripped META.
  rocq-micromega-plugin.plugin
  rocq-micromega-plugin.zify))
